1 TITL The Liebes Family: Jewish San Francisco Importers and Manufacturers of Fur Products
1 AUTH Jewish Museum of the American West (JMAW)
1 PUBL jmaw.org
1 _URL https://www.jmaw.org/liebes-jewish-fur-san-francisco/
1 _CONF Tentative
1 _ACC 2026-07-11
1 NOTE Background on the prominent Liebes family of San Francisco: Herman Liebes
2 CONT (b. ~1842, German-Jewish immigrant) founded H. Liebes & Co., a leading Pacific
2 CONT fur house ("indisputably the largest dealers in sealskins in the world,"
2 CONT 1898-99 catalogue); active in B'nai B'rith and Congregation Emanu-El. Recorded
2 CONT as a RESEARCH LEAD for Joan Liebes's ancestry (Ashkenazi, early life in SF) -
2 CONT no proven connection yet.
